%description:
Tests a SYN with a flag combination that RFC 9768 does not define: the tester
changes the classic ECN-setup SYN to ACE 0b101. An AccECN server negotiates
AccECN as for (1,1,1) (section 3.1.3) and sends ACE 0b010. The classic client
sees no ECE and uses no ECN, so its ACK of the SYN-ACK has ACE 0b000. Then the
server sets no ECT and ignores the feedback (Table 4), but it still sends the
ACE field.

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
record-vector-results = false
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib

cmdenv-event-banners=false
cmdenv-express-mode=false

*.testing=true
cmdenv-log-prefix="[%c]: "

*.cli_app.sendScript="1.0 1000"
*.*_tcp.accEcnOptionEnabled = false # the ACE field alone (tcp_accecn_option_* test the option)
*.cli_tcp.tcpEcnMode = "rfc3168"
*.srv_tcp.tcpEcnMode = "accecn"
*.tcptester.script="a1 ace 5"

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%file: postrun.pl
open FILE, '<test.out';
while($sor = <FILE>)
{
    if ($sor =~ /^\[testing\]: (.*)$/)
    {
        print "$1\n";
    }
}
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command:  perl ./postrun.pl
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: postrun-command(1).out
[0.001 A001] A.1000 > B.2000: S E N 0:0(0) win 16384   Option(s): MaxSegSize# changing ACE bits
srv_tcp: LISTEN --> SYN_RCVD  (on RCV_SYN)
[0.003 B001] A.1000 < B.2000: A S W 500:500(0) ack 1 win 16384   Option(s): MaxSegSize
cli_tcp: SYN_SENT --> ESTABLISHED  (on RCV_SYN_ACK)
[0.005 A002] A.1000 > B.2000: A ack 501 win 16384 
srv_tcp: SYN_RCVD --> ESTABLISHED  (on RCV_ACK)
[1.001 A003] A.1000 > B.2000: A 1:1001(1000) ack 501 win 16384 
[1.203 B002] A.1000 < B.2000: A E N ack 1001 win 16384 
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: stdout
AccECN: the ACK of the SYN-ACK has ACE 0, no ECT and no response to the feedback
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command: grep "undisposed object:" test.out > test_undisposed.out || true
%not-contains: test_undisposed.out
undisposed object: (
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
